ines and positions on various aspects of nutrition, including dietary practices for older adults in long-term care settings, nutrition interventions for the treatment of eating disorders, and resources for managing specific conditions such as dysphagia. Additionally, the organization addresses the nutritional needs of patients with specific health conditions, including those with dementia, ensuring that dietitians and nutritionists have access to the necessary tools and information to support their clients effectively.\",8\r\n8621,ANOREXIA NERVOSA,\"Anorexia Nervosa (AN) is a serious psychological condition and a specific type of restrictive eating disorder characterized by an intense fear of gaining weight and a distorted body image. This disorder leads individuals to significantly restrict their food intake, resulting in severe weight loss and various health complications. The intense fear of weight gain and the distorted perception of body image are central to the condition, making it a complex and challenging disorder to treat. Anorexia Nervosa is contraindicated for the use of certain treatments, such as BN, highlighting the need for specialized care in managing this serious eating disorder.\",33\r\n4730,JOURNAL OF CLINICAL ENDOCRINOLOGY AND METABOLISM,\"The Journal of Clinical Endocrinology and Metabolism is a prominent medical journal dedicated to publishing research on various aspects of endocrinology and metabolism. It covers a wide range of topics, including the impacts of diet on health, endocrine disorders such as medullary thyroid carcinoma, and hormonal and metabolic disorders. The journal features studies on vitamin D deficiency in cystic fibrosis patients, as well as research related to anorexia nervosa and its treatments. Through its diverse array of publications, the Journal of Clinical Endocrinology and Metabolism contributes significantly to the understanding and advancement of knowledge in the fields of endocrinology and metabolism.\",4\r\n6783,